<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vsevolod Mstislavich of Belz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">12th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vsevolod-mstislavich">Vsevolod Mstislavich</a> was a prince of the Volhynian branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rurik-dynasty">Rurikids</a>, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mstislav-ii-of-kiev">Mstislav II of Kiev</a> and brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-the-great">Roman Mstislavich</a>. In the later 12th century he ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belz">Belz</a> as an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appanage">appanage</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volhynia">Volhynia</a>, making the town the seat of a small principality on the border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>.</p></div>
